CHECKS: 7/7 passed
VERDICT (against the declared criteria):
  * The dS_2 fermion induced current is computed by a direct mode sum and matches the published closed form (V1-V4).
  * It carries e^2: sigma H = (e^2/H^2) g_f(mu), g_f = 2 mu/sinh(2 pi mu), mass dependent; only lambda = eE/H^2 enters the nonlinear function.
  * Massless limit: J = e^2 E/(pi H) exactly for all lambda (the anomaly); g_f(0) = 1/pi = the coefficient of the Schwinger-model photon mass e^2/pi.
  * Unlike the scalar: no 1/(2 pi mu^2) divergence at small mu; at large mu g_f/g_s -> exp(-pi/(4 mu)).
  * A tie sigma/H = c fixes e^2/H^2 = pi c only for an exactly massless fermion with c supplied from outside; for any massive fermion the required coupling
    varies over many decades (V6).  2D toy: e has mass dimension 1; dS_4 fermions and charge renormalisation are not computed here.
  * kappa = 1/2 stays FITTED.  The SM-mass wall is unchanged.
exit 0
